/-!
# The differentials of the small resolution of a semifree differential graded path algebra

Let `Q` be a quiver with finitely many vertices, `k` a commutative ring, and `(kQ, d)` a
differential graded path algebra: the path algebra graded by an integer weight `wt` on the arrows,
with a differential `d` of degree one which kills the vertex idempotents. As a graded algebra `kQ`
is free over the vertex subalgebra `kQ₀` on the arrows, so `(kQ, d)` is semifree; the
two-dimensional Ginzburg algebra `Π₂(Q)`, with `TauCeti.ginzburgTwoDifferential`, is an example.

The standard sequence of `kQ`-bimodules

```text
0 ⟶ ⨁_{b : i ⟶ j} kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ ⟶ kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ ⟶ kQ ⟶ 0
```

of `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorDifferential` (written `δ` below) and
`TauCeti.PathAlgebra.vertexTensorMul` is short exact. This file equips its two left terms with
differentials which square to zero and for which both maps are chain maps, so that the sequence
becomes a short exact sequence of complexes of bimodules. These are the differentials of the small
bimodule resolution of `(kQ, d)`, the cone of `δ`, through which the Hochschild cohomology of a
semifree algebra such as `Π₂(Q)` is computed. The gradings of the two terms and the cone itself are
not constructed here.

* On `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ`, generated by `∑ᵥ eᵥ ⊗ eᵥ` in degree zero, the differential is
  `x ⊗ y ↦ d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ |x| x ⊗ d y`.
* On `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ` the generator `s_b = ∂b` of the component of an arrow `b` has degree
  `|b|`, where `∂` is the universal derivation `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorDerivation`, and the
  differential is twisted by `s_b ↦ ∂ (d b)`:

  ```text
  d (x s_b y) = d x s_b y + (-1) ^ |x| x ∂(d b) y + (-1) ^ (|x| + |b|) x s_b d y.
  ```

  The twist is the term which makes `δ`, sending `s_b` to `b ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ b`, a chain map. With it,
  `∂` is a chain map as well.

The elements of both bimodules are elements of the enveloping algebra `kQ ⊗[k] kQᵐᵒᵖ`, and both
differentials come from `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.envelopeDifferential`, the differential
`x ⊗ y ↦ d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ (|x| + n) x ⊗ d y` of the free bimodule on a cycle of degree `n`. The
sign `(-1) ^ |x|` is the Koszul twist `TauCeti.InternalGrading.koszulTwist`, which makes the
formulas meaningful for inhomogeneous `x`. Identities in `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ` are proved after
applying the injective map `δ`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.envelopeDifferential`: the differential of the free bimodule on a cycle of
  degree `n`, on the enveloping algebra.
* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential`: the differential of `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ`.
* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential`: the twisted differential of
  `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_smul_arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow`: the
  twisted differential on the generators.
* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.envelopeDifferential_envelopeDifferential`,
  `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential` and
  `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential`: **the
  differentials square to zero**.
* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential` and
  `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.vertexTensorMul_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential`: **the maps of the
  standard sequence are chain maps**.
* `TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation`: **the universal
  derivation is a chain map**, `d (∂ y) = ∂ (d y)`.

## References

* D. Happel, *Hochschild cohomology of finite-dimensional algebras*, Séminaire d'Algèbre Paul
  Dubreil et Marie-Paul Malliavin, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1404 (1989), 108--126, for the
  standard bimodule resolution of a path algebra.
* B. Keller, *Deformed Calabi--Yau completions*, J. Reine Angew. Math. 654 (2011), 125--180,
  arXiv:0908.3499, for semifree differential graded algebras, Ginzburg algebras and their bimodule
  resolutions.
* Y. Liu and W. Wang, *A-infinity deformations of zigzag algebras via Ginzburg dg algebras*,
  arXiv:2301.06757, for the Hochschild cohomology of the two-dimensional Ginzburg algebra.
-/

public section

open MulOpposite
open scoped TensorProduct DirectSum

namespace TauCeti

namespace PathAlgebra

universe u v w

variable {k : Type w} [CommRing k] {Q : Type u} [Quiver.{v} Q] [Finite Q]

/-- The path algebra, in this file. -/
local notation "𝒜" => pathAlgebra k Q

/-- The enveloping algebra of the path algebra, in this file. -/
local notation "𝒜ᵉ" => pathAlgebra k Q ⊗[k] (pathAlgebra k Q)ᵐᵒᵖ

/-- The vertex idempotent `eᵥ`, in this file. -/
local notation "ε" => vertexIdempotent k

variable (wt : ∀ {a b : Q}, (a ⟶ b) → ℤ) (d : pathAlgebra k Q →ₗ[k] pathAlgebra k Q)

/-- The grading sign `x ↦ (-1) ^ |x| x` of the grading by `wt`, in this file. -/
local notation "σ" =>
  InternalGrading.koszulTwist (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (gradeBy k wt)) 1

/-- A linear endomorphism of the path algebra, transported to the opposite algebra, in this
file. -/
local notation "op[" f "]" =>
  LinearMap.comp (LinearEquiv.toLinearMap (opLinearEquiv k))
    (LinearMap.comp f (LinearEquiv.toLinearMap (LinearEquiv.symm (opLinearEquiv k))))

/-! ### The grading sign -/

section Sign

variable {wt}

private theorem sign_apply_of_mem {m : ℤ} {x : 𝒜} (hx : x ∈ gradeBy k wt m) :
    σ x = negOnePowCast k m • x := by
  rw [InternalGrading.koszulTwist_one_apply_of_mem _
    (by rwa [InternalGrading.ofDecomposition_piece]), negOnePowCast_eq_intCast]

private theorem sign_vertexIdempotent (v : Q) : σ (ε v) = ε v := by
  rw [sign_apply_of_mem (vertexIdempotent_mem_gradeBy_zero wt v), negOnePowCast_zero, one_smul]

private theorem sign_one : σ (1 : 𝒜) = 1 := by
  rw [sign_apply_of_mem (SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := gradeBy k wt)), negOnePowCast_zero,
    one_smul]

end Sign

/-! ### The differential of the enveloping algebra -/

section Envelope

/-- **The differential of the free bimodule on one generator of degree `n`**, written on the
enveloping algebra `kQ ⊗[k] kQᵐᵒᵖ` of a differential graded path algebra: for `x` homogeneous of
degree `|x|`, it sends `x ⊗ y` to `d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ (|x| + n) x ⊗ d y`
(`TauCeti.PathAlgebra.envelopeDifferential_tmul_of_mem`). It is the differential of
`x s y ↦ x ⊗ y` for a generator `s` of degree `n` which is a cycle, and it squares to zero
(`TauCeti.PathAlgebra.envelopeDifferential_envelopeDifferential`). -/
noncomputable def envelopeDifferential (n : ℤ) : 𝒜ᵉ →ₗ[k] 𝒜ᵉ :=
  TensorProduct.map d LinearMap.id + negOnePowCast k n • TensorProduct.map σ op[d]

variable {wt d}

/-- **The differential of the free bimodule on a generator of degree `n`** on a pure tensor:
`d (x ⊗ y) = d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ n σ x ⊗ d y`, for `σ` the Koszul twist `x ↦ (-1) ^ |x| x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem envelopeDifferential_tmul (n : ℤ) (x y : 𝒜) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (x ⊗ₜ[k] op y) =
      d x ⊗ₜ[k] op y + negOnePowCast k n • (σ x ⊗ₜ[k] op (d y)) := by
  simp [envelopeDifferential]

/-- The differential of the free bimodule on a generator of degree `n` on a pure tensor with
homogeneous left factor: `d (x ⊗ y) = d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ (|x| + n) x ⊗ d y`. -/
theorem envelopeDifferential_tmul_of_mem (n : ℤ) {p : ℤ} {x : 𝒜} (hx : x ∈ gradeBy k wt p)
    (y : 𝒜) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (x ⊗ₜ[k] op y) =
      d x ⊗ₜ[k] op y + negOnePowCast k (p + n) • (x ⊗ₜ[k] op (d y)) := by
  rw [envelopeDifferential_tmul, sign_apply_of_mem hx, ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_smul,
    ← negOnePowCast_add, add_comm n p]

/-- The Leibniz rule of the enveloping differential, with the sign of the right factor spelled
out by the grading sign on both of its tensor factors. -/
private theorem envelopeDifferential_mul (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (n : ℤ)
    (u v : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (u * v) =
      TensorProduct.map d LinearMap.id u * v +
        TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id u * envelopeDifferential wt d n v +
          negOnePowCast k n •
            (TensorProduct.map σ op[d] u * TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] v) := by
  induction u using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add u u' hu hu' => simp only [add_mul, map_add, hu, hu', smul_add]; abel
  | tmul x y =>
    induction v using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | add v v' hv hv' => simp only [mul_add, map_add, hv, hv', smul_add]; abel
    | tmul x' y' =>
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (opLinearEquiv k).surjective y
      obtain ⟨y', rfl⟩ := (opLinearEquiv k).surjective y'
      simp only [coe_opLinearEquiv, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, ← op_mul,
        envelopeDifferential_tmul, TensorProduct.map_tmul, LinearMap.id_apply,
        LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, coe_opLinearEquiv_symm, unop_op,
        hd.toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.leibniz_koszulTwist,
        InternalGrading.koszulTwist_ofDecomposition_mul, op_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add,
        TensorProduct.add_tmul,
        smul_add, mul_add, mul_smul_comm]
      abel

private theorem envelopeDifferential_mul_of_sign (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (n m : ℤ)
    {v : 𝒜ᵉ} (hv : TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] v = negOnePowCast k m • v) (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (u * v) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d (n + m) u * v +
        TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id u * envelopeDifferential wt d n v := by
  rw [envelopeDifferential_mul hd, hv, mul_smul_comm, smul_smul, ← negOnePowCast_add]
  simp only [envelopeDifferential, LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, add_mul,
    smul_mul_assoc]
  abel

/-- **The enveloping differential squares to zero.** -/
@[simp]
theorem envelopeDifferential_envelopeDifferential (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (n : ℤ)
    (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (envelopeDifferential wt d n u) = 0 := by
  induction u using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add u u' hu hu' => rw [map_add, map_add, hu, hu', add_zero]
  | tmul x y =>
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (opLinearEquiv k).surjective y
    simp only [coe_opLinearEquiv, envelopeDifferential_tmul, map_add, map_smul, hd.sq_zero,
      hd.toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.map_koszulTwist, InternalGrading.koszulTwist_koszulTwist, op_zero,
      TensorProduct.tmul_zero, TensorProduct.zero_tmul, smul_zero, add_zero, zero_add,
      TensorProduct.neg_tmul, smul_neg]
    abel

end Envelope

/-! ### Vertex idempotents -/

section Idempotent

variable {wt d}

private theorem map_sign_op_tmul_vertexIdempotent (v w : Q) :
    TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] (ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w)) = ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w) := by
  simp [sign_vertexIdempotent]

private theorem map_sign_id_mul_tmul_vertexIdempotent (v w : Q) (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id (u * (ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w))) =
      TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id u * (ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w)) := by
  induction u using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul x y => simp [InternalGrading.koszulTwist_ofDecomposition_mul, sign_vertexIdempotent]
  | add u u' hu hu' => rw [add_mul, map_add, hu, hu', map_add, add_mul]

private theorem envelopeDifferential_mul_tmul_vertexIdempotent
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (n : ℤ) (v w : Q) (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (u * (ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w))) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d n u * (ε v ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε w)) := by
  rw [envelopeDifferential_mul_of_sign hd n 0
      (by rw [map_sign_op_tmul_vertexIdempotent, negOnePowCast_zero, one_smul]),
    add_zero, envelopeDifferential_tmul, hdε, hdε, op_zero, TensorProduct.tmul_zero,
    TensorProduct.zero_tmul, smul_zero, add_zero, mul_zero, add_zero]

/-- A differential killing the vertex idempotents preserves the corner `eⱼ (kQ) eᵢ` of an arrow
`b : i ⟶ j`. -/
private theorem vertexIdempotent_mul_mul_vertexIdempotent (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d)
    (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) {i j : Q} (b : i ⟶ j) :
    ε j * d (ofArrow b) * ε i = d (ofArrow b) := by
  have hl := hd.toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.leibniz_koszulTwist (ε j) (ofArrow b)
  have hr := hd.toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.leibniz_koszulTwist (ofArrow b) (ε i)
  rw [vertexIdempotent_mul_ofArrow_self, hdε, zero_mul, zero_add, sign_vertexIdempotent] at hl
  rw [ofArrow_mul_vertexIdempotent_self, hdε, mul_zero, add_zero] at hr
  rw [← hl, ← hr]

end Idempotent

/-! ### The twisted differential of the left term -/

section Arrow

variable [DecidableEq Q] [∀ i j : Q, DecidableEq (i ⟶ j)]

omit [DecidableEq Q] [∀ i j : Q, DecidableEq (i ⟶ j)] in
/-- `mul_smul` for the action of the enveloping algebra on `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ`, stated with the
action as it elaborates on that direct sum: `rw [smul_smul]` does not find this instance path
syntactically, although it is definitionally the `MulAction` one. -/
private theorem smul_smul_arrowTensorBimodule (x y : 𝒜ᵉ) (w : arrowTensorBimodule k Q) :
    x • y • w = (x * y) • w :=
  (mul_smul x y w).symm

/-- The universal derivation of an element of a corner `eⱼ (kQ) eᵢ` is cut down by `eⱼ ⊗ eᵢ`. -/
private theorem arrowTensorDerivation_vertexIdempotent_mul_mul (i j : Q) (z : 𝒜) :
    arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ε j * z * ε i) =
      (ε j ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε i) : 𝒜ᵉ) • arrowTensorDerivation k Q z := by
  rw [arrowTensorDerivation_mul, arrowTensorDerivation_mul, arrowTensorDerivation_vertexIdempotent,
    arrowTensorDerivation_vertexIdempotent, smul_zero, smul_zero, add_zero, zero_add]
  rw [smul_smul_arrowTensorBimodule, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul]

/-- The twisted differential on the component of an arrow `b`: `u ↦ D u • ∂b + σ u • ∂(d b)` for
`D` the enveloping differential in the degree of `b` and `σ` the grading sign on the left factor. -/
private noncomputable def arrowTensorComponentDifferential (b : Σ i j : Q, i ⟶ j) :
    (Ideal.span {arrowTensorIdempotent k Q b} : Ideal 𝒜ᵉ) →ₗ[k] arrowTensorBimodule k Q :=
  ((LinearMap.toSpanSingleton 𝒜ᵉ _ (arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b.2.2))).restrictScalars k ∘ₗ
      envelopeDifferential wt d (wt b.2.2) +
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton 𝒜ᵉ _
        (arrowTensorDerivation k Q (d (ofArrow b.2.2)))).restrictScalars k ∘ₗ
      TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id) ∘ₗ
    (Ideal.span {arrowTensorIdempotent k Q b}).subtype.restrictScalars k

/-- **The twisted differential of `⨁_{b : i ⟶ j} kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ`** for a differential graded path
algebra `(kQ, d)`, graded by the arrow weight `wt`. Writing `s_b = ∂b` for the generator of the
component of an arrow `b`, of degree `|b|`, it is
`d (x s_b y) = d x s_b y + (-1) ^ |x| x ∂(d b) y + (-1) ^ (|x| + |b|) x s_b d y`
(`TauCeti.PathAlgebra.arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_smul_arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow`): the
differential of the free bimodule on the generators `s_b`, twisted by `s_b ↦ ∂(d b)`. -/
noncomputable def arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential :
    arrowTensorBimodule k Q →ₗ[k] arrowTensorBimodule k Q :=
  DirectSum.toModule k _ _ (arrowTensorComponentDifferential wt d)

variable {wt d}

/-- **The twisted differential on the generators**: on `u s_b`, for `s_b = ∂b` the generator of
the component of an arrow `b` and `u` in the enveloping algebra, it is the enveloping differential
of `u` in the degree of `b`, times `s_b`, plus the grading sign of the left factor of `u` times
`∂(d b)`. -/
theorem arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_smul_arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (u : 𝒜ᵉ) {i j : Q}
    (b : i ⟶ j) :
    arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d (u • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b)) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d (wt b) u • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b) +
        TensorProduct.map σ LinearMap.id u • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (d (ofArrow b)) := by
  have hgen : u • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b) =
      DirectSum.lof k _ (fun b ↦ (Ideal.span {arrowTensorIdempotent k Q b} : Ideal 𝒜ᵉ)) ⟨i, j, b⟩
        (u • spanSingletonGenerator (arrowTensorIdempotent k Q ⟨i, j, b⟩)) := by
    rw [arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow, ← map_smul, DirectSum.lof_eq_of, DirectSum.lof_eq_of]
  have hb : (ε j ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε i) : 𝒜ᵉ) • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b) =
      arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b) := by
    rw [← arrowTensorDerivation_vertexIdempotent_mul_mul, vertexIdempotent_mul_ofArrow_self,
      ofArrow_mul_vertexIdempotent_self]
  have hdb : (ε j ⊗ₜ[k] op (ε i) : 𝒜ᵉ) • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (d (ofArrow b)) =
      arrowTensorDerivation k Q (d (ofArrow b)) := by
    rw [← arrowTensorDerivation_vertexIdempotent_mul_mul,
      vertexIdempotent_mul_mul_vertexIdempotent hd hdε]
  rw [hgen, arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential, DirectSum.toModule_lof]
  simp only [arrowTensorComponentDifferential, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.add_apply,
    LinearMap.restrictScalars_apply, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply,
    Submodule.coe_smul, smul_eq_mul, coe_spanSingletonGenerator, arrowTensorIdempotent_def]
  rw [envelopeDifferential_mul_tmul_vertexIdempotent hd hdε, map_sign_id_mul_tmul_vertexIdempotent,
    ← smul_smul_arrowTensorBimodule, ← smul_smul_arrowTensorBimodule, hb, hdb]

end Arrow

/-! ### The differential of the middle term and the chain maps -/

section Vertex

variable [Fintype Q]

/-- **The differential of `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ`** for a differential graded path algebra `(kQ, d)`: the
enveloping differential `x ⊗ y ↦ d x ⊗ y + (-1) ^ |x| x ⊗ d y` of the generator `∑ᵥ eᵥ ⊗ eᵥ` of
degree zero, cut down to the left ideal generated by that idempotent. When `d` kills the vertex
idempotents the cut is not needed (`TauCeti.PathAlgebra.coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential`). -/
noncomputable def vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential :
    vertexTensorBimodule k Q →ₗ[k] vertexTensorBimodule k Q where
  toFun u := ⟨envelopeDifferential wt d 0 u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q,
    mem_vertexTensorBimodule_iff.2 (by
      rw [mul_assoc, (isIdempotentElem_vertexTensorIdempotent k Q).eq])⟩
  map_add' u u' := by ext; simp [add_mul]
  map_smul' c u := by ext; simp [smul_mul_assoc]

variable {wt d}

private theorem coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential_apply (u : vertexTensorBimodule k Q) :
    (vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d u : 𝒜ᵉ) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d 0 u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q := (rfl)

private theorem envelopeDifferential_mul_vertexTensorIdempotent
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (n : ℤ) (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d n (u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d n u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q := by
  simp only [vertexTensorIdempotent_def, Finset.mul_sum, map_sum,
    envelopeDifferential_mul_tmul_vertexIdempotent hd hdε]

/-- When `d` kills the vertex idempotents, the differential of `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ` is the enveloping
differential in degree zero. -/
theorem coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d)
    (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (u : vertexTensorBimodule k Q) :
    (vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d u : 𝒜ᵉ) = envelopeDifferential wt d 0 u := by
  rw [coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential_apply,
    ← envelopeDifferential_mul_vertexTensorIdempotent hd hdε,
    mem_vertexTensorBimodule_iff.1 u.2]

/-- **The differential of `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ` squares to zero.** -/
@[simp]
theorem vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (u : vertexTensorBimodule k Q) :
    vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d (vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d u) = 0 := by
  ext
  rw [coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε, coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε,
    envelopeDifferential_envelopeDifferential hd, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero]

/-- **The multiplication map is a chain map**: it intertwines the differential of
`kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ` with `d`. -/
theorem vertexTensorMul_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d)
    (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (u : vertexTensorBimodule k Q) :
    vertexTensorMul k Q (vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d u) =
      Bimodule.of (AlgHom.id k 𝒜)
        (d ((Bimodule.of (AlgHom.id k 𝒜)).symm (vertexTensorMul k Q u))) := by
  rw [vertexTensorMul_apply, vertexTensorMul_apply, coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε]
  induction (u : 𝒜ᵉ) using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul x y =>
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (opLinearEquiv k).surjective y
    simp [envelopeDifferential_tmul, Bimodule.smul_of, add_smul,
      hd.toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.leibniz_koszulTwist]
  | add u u' hu hu' => rw [map_add, add_smul, hu, hu', add_smul, map_add, map_add, map_add]

private theorem map_sign_op_mul_vertexTensorIdempotent (u : 𝒜ᵉ) :
    TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] (u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q) =
      TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] u * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q := by
  induction u using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul x y =>
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (opLinearEquiv k).surjective y
    simp [vertexTensorIdempotent_def, Finset.mul_sum, ← op_mul,
      InternalGrading.koszulTwist_ofDecomposition_mul, sign_vertexIdempotent]
  | add u u' hu hu' => rw [add_mul, map_add, hu, hu', map_add, add_mul]

/-- The boundary `(y ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ y)(∑ᵥ eᵥ ⊗ eᵥ)` of the universal derivation of a homogeneous `y`
carries the grading sign of `y` on both tensor factors. -/
private theorem map_sign_op_boundary {m : ℤ} {y : 𝒜} (hy : y ∈ gradeBy k wt m) :
    TensorProduct.map σ op[σ] ((y ⊗ₜ[k] 1 - 1 ⊗ₜ[k] op y) * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q) =
      negOnePowCast k m • ((y ⊗ₜ[k] 1 - 1 ⊗ₜ[k] op y) * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q) := by
  rw [map_sign_op_mul_vertexTensorIdempotent, ← smul_mul_assoc, ← op_one, map_sub,
    TensorProduct.map_tmul, TensorProduct.map_tmul]
  simp [sign_apply_of_mem hy, sign_one, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_sub]

/-- The enveloping differential of `y ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ y` is `d y ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ d y`. -/
private theorem envelopeDifferential_boundary (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d)
    (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (y : 𝒜) :
    envelopeDifferential wt d 0 ((y ⊗ₜ[k] 1 - 1 ⊗ₜ[k] op y) * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q) =
      (d y ⊗ₜ[k] 1 - 1 ⊗ₜ[k] op (d y)) * vertexTensorIdempotent k Q := by
  rw [envelopeDifferential_mul_vertexTensorIdempotent hd hdε, ← op_one, map_sub,
    envelopeDifferential_tmul, envelopeDifferential_tmul, hd.map_one_eq_zero, sign_one]
  simp

variable [DecidableEq Q] [∀ i j : Q, DecidableEq (i ⟶ j)]

/-- **The differential of the standard resolution is a chain map**, as a map into the enveloping
algebra: it intertwines the twisted differential of `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ` with the enveloping
differential in degree zero. -/
theorem coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (w : arrowTensorBimodule k Q) :
    (arrowTensorDifferential k Q (arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d w) : 𝒜ᵉ) =
      envelopeDifferential wt d 0 (arrowTensorDifferential k Q w) := by
  induction w using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add w w' hw hw' => rw [map_add, map_add, Submodule.coe_add, hw, hw', map_add,
      Submodule.coe_add, map_add]
  | of b u =>
    obtain ⟨i, j, b⟩ := b
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := u
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hu
    have hof : DirectSum.of (fun b ↦ (Ideal.span {arrowTensorIdempotent k Q b} : Ideal 𝒜ᵉ))
        ⟨i, j, b⟩ ⟨v * arrowTensorIdempotent k Q ⟨i, j, b⟩, hu⟩ =
        v • arrowTensorDerivation k Q (ofArrow b) := by
      rw [arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow, ← map_smul, DirectSum.lof_eq_of]
      congr 1
      exact Subtype.ext (by rw [SetLike.val_smul, coe_spanSingletonGenerator, smul_eq_mul])
    rw [hof, arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_smul_arrowTensorDerivation_ofArrow hd hdε, map_add,
      map_smul, map_smul, map_smul, Submodule.coe_add, Submodule.coe_smul, Submodule.coe_smul,
      Submodule.coe_smul, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul,
      coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation,
      coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation,
      envelopeDifferential_mul_of_sign hd 0 (wt b)
        (map_sign_op_boundary (ofArrow_mem_gradeBy wt b)),
      zero_add, envelopeDifferential_boundary hd hdε]

/-- **The differential of the standard resolution is a chain map**: it intertwines the twisted
differential of `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ` with the differential of `kQ ⊗_{kQ₀} kQ`. -/
theorem arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (w : arrowTensorBimodule k Q) :
    arrowTensorDifferential k Q (arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d w) =
      vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d (arrowTensorDifferential k Q w) :=
  Subtype.ext (by rw [coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε,
    coe_vertexTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε])

end Vertex

section Square

variable [DecidableEq Q] [∀ i j : Q, DecidableEq (i ⟶ j)]

variable {wt d}

/-- **The twisted differential squares to zero.** -/
@[simp]
theorem arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (w : arrowTensorBimodule k Q) :
    arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d (arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d w) = 0 := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite Q
  refine arrowTensorDifferential_injective (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε,
    coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε,
    envelopeDifferential_envelopeDifferential hd, map_zero, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero]

/-- **The universal derivation is a chain map**: `d (∂ y) = ∂ (d y)` for the twisted differential
of `⨁_b kQ eⱼ ⊗_k eᵢ kQ`. -/
theorem arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation
    (hd : IsDGAlgebra (gradeBy k wt) d) (hdε : ∀ v, d (ε v) = 0) (y : 𝒜) :
    arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential wt d (arrowTensorDerivation k Q y) =
      arrowTensorDerivation k Q (d y) := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite Q
  refine arrowTensorDifferential_injective (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorBimoduleDifferential hd hdε,
    coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation,
    coe_arrowTensorDifferential_arrowTensorDerivation, envelopeDifferential_boundary hd hdε]

end Square

